  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Susanth Kumar Roht Susantha Rao, vs State Of Ap on 16 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.4895 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioner/accused seeks to quash the proceedings against him in C.C.No.1813 of 2019 on the file of Special Judicial First Class Magistrate for Prohibition & Excise, Guntur, which was taken cognizance for the offences under Sections 270, 273 and 284 of IPC and Sections 57(1) and 58 of Food Safety and Standards Act (for short, 'FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that on 23.04.2019 at 12.30 p.m., when the complainant along with his staff reached 1st Lane, Krishna Nagar, on suspicion, caught the accused and found the banned tobacco products in their possession and hence, seized the same and registered a case in Crime No.182 of 2019 of Pattabhipuram Police Station, Guntur Urban, for the offences stated supra. 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
